Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.39,0:00:06.15,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,When it comes to cleaning up...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.48,0:00:12.61,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,I'm very thorough!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.20,0:00:14.70,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fs10\shad0\blur4\c&H486065&\3c&HEFF5F2&\b1\pos(221.51,230)}Bodyguard & Maid,\NPreviously in Prince Osvalt's Service\N{\fs18} Lena
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.70,0:00:17.41,Default,Leonardo,0,0,0,,Indeed, in all respects...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.74,0:00:19.44,Default,Leonardo,0,0,0,,We must be flawless!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.32,0:00:24.64,Default,Leonardo,0,0,0,,That is a butler's job.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.92,0:00:26.33,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fs10\shad0\blur4\c&H486065&\3c&HEFF5F2&\b1\pos(221.51,230)}Bodyguard, Butler & Former Knight,\NPreviously in Prince Osvalt's Service\N{\fs16}Leonardo
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.77,0:00:30.61,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Parnacorta is famous for the \Nexcellence of its chivalric order.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.98,0:00:30.13,Main - Top,Leonardo,0,0,0,,Prepare to die!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.61,0:00:34.68,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Perhaps they instruct even their \Nbutlers and maids in martial arts.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.68,0:00:38.39,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\an9\fnArial\b1\shad0\pos(455.959,26.42)\blur3\c&H25373B&\3c&HE4FDFD&}No, They're Just Weird
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.96,0:00:38.39,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}But even then...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.28,0:00:41.53,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}These two are {\i0}really{\i1} tough.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.29,0:01:05.92,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(710,1)\blur4\t(1,710,\blur0)\an8\fnGeorgia\b1\fs18\shad0\bord0\c&HDA8FA9&}The Too-Perfect Saint: Tossed Aside\Nby My Fiancé and Sold to Another Kingdom
Dialogue: 1,0:01:03.93,0:01:05.94,Default,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(960,1)\an8\fnGeorgia\b1\fs18\shad0\bord0\c&H884FD9&\3c&HFCFEFE&}The Too-Perfect Saint{\c&H9B9999&}: {\c&HDEC58D&}Tossed {\c&HDDBF93&}Aside\N{\c&HE2B99A&}by {\c&HC8ACAD&}My {\c&HDDB3B4&}Fiancé {\c&HDCBAC3&}and {\c&HD79BB3&}Sold {\c&HCEA8CE&}to {\c&HD4A8D5&}Another {\c&HC3A8E2&}Kingdom
Dialogue: 1,0:02:13.11,0:02:14.62,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,Saint Philia!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.11,0:02:20.24,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(690,1)\shad1\bord0\fnGeorgia\fs10\c&HF9F8FA&\3c&H4E4E4E&\4c&H252526&\pos(513.632,283.044)}Episode 3\N{\fs12}"Our First {\fs12\c&H635CF4&}Date{\fs10\c&HFBFFFF&\4c&H6A6763&}"
Dialogue: 1,0:02:14.62,0:02:16.76,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,The cleaning's all done!
Dialogue: 1,0:02:16.76,0:02:20.24,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Excellent work. You're both phenomenal.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.73,0:02:21.82,Default,Leonardo,0,0,0,,Oh, hardly.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.82,0:02:24.96,Default,Leonardo,0,0,0,,The monsters were already weakened \Ndue to the holy sanctuary.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.96,0:02:26.20,Default,Leonardo,0,0,0,,Besides...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.20,0:02:40.78,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\bord1.5\shad0\fnArial\fs20\b1\c&H1E62F9&\3c&HD4FAFD&\pos(255.669,228.63)}Extremely
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.20,0:02:40.78,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnArial\fs20\b1\c&HA9FFF5&\3c&H278CD6&\pos(415.503,242.553)\4c&H71B7CC&}Effective
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.20,0:02:44.72,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnArial\fs18\b1\shad0\pos(318.673,60.895)\c&H3968AE&\3c&HB2FFFE&}Mental Image
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.68,0:02:33.87,Default,Leonardo,0,0,0,,That potion you gave me makes me \Nfeel like I'm back in my heyday!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.87,0:02:36.21,Default,Leonardo,0,0,0,,Plus, look at how dark \Nand full my hair has gotten!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.54,0:02:38.96,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,I'm feeling on the top of my game, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.96,0:02:41.05,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,You're amazing, Saint Philia!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.05,0:02:44.72,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,It was just a rudimentary potion, though...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.72,0:02:47.81,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,Actually, I've been wondering something.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.81,0:02:50.60,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,What have you been jotting down?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.60,0:02:52.96,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Oh, this?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.70,0:02:59.36,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,I'm recording information on the location, \Nscale, and ferocity of monster outbreaks.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.36,0:03:03.36,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,It sure does seem like\N they've been on the rise, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.36,0:03:07.07,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,Even when we wipe them out, \Nthey come back in no time.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.07,0:03:09.37,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,What's up with that?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.37,0:03:11.04,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Well, you see...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.34,0:03:15.58,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,In addition to the surface world\Nwhich we humans inhabit,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.58,0:03:17.67,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,there exist the Demon Realm and Heaven.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.26,0:03:21.36,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Monsters are native to the Demon Realm,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.36,0:03:24.68,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,but sometimes a portion of them \Nmake it up here to the surface.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.68,0:03:27.37,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,Just a portion? But there's been so many...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:27.37,0:03:32.23,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Yes. The more nests in the Demon Realm, \Nthe more monsters there are,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.23,0:03:35.60,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,which in turn means more \Nand more frequent surface invasions.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.08,0:03:38.30,Default,Leonardo,0,0,0,,Saint Philia.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.10,0:03:41.24,Default,Leonardo,0,0,0,,The carriage is ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.68,0:03:43.54,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Let's return to the mansion.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.54,0:03:44.43,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,Yes, ma'am!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.43,0:03:48.95,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,By the way, Saint Philia,\Nwe're done for the day now, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.95,0:03:50.16,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Yes. What of it?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.16,0:03:51.66,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,In that case...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.76,0:03:54.29,Default,Shopkeepers,0,0,0,,Prince Osvalt!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.29,0:03:56.14,Default,Shopkeepers,0,0,0,,Good to see you!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.14,0:03:59.24,Default,Greengrocer,0,0,0,,Highness! Take some of my vegetables!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.24,0:04:00.84,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Sure, I'll stop by later.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.84,0:04:02.45,Default,Greengrocer,0,0,0,,Oh, out on business now?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.45,0:04:03.26,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.74,0:04:05.93,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,I'm off on a date.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.83,0:04:09.18,Default,Shopkeepers,0,0,0,,A d-date?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.45,0:04:11.68,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Miss Philia!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.68,0:04:13.26,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,I tried to come ea—
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.52,0:04:22.32,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Sorry. Guess I kept you waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.88,0:04:24.56,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Not at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.78,0:04:29.24,Flashback,Lena,0,0,0,,Let's make it a date!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.24,0:04:31.77,Flashback,Philia,0,0,0,,A d-date?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.77,0:04:35.40,Flashback,Philia,0,0,0,,I've heard the word before, \Nbut I don't know what it entails.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.40,0:04:40.32,Flashback,Lena,0,0,0,,For today, how about a tour of Almburg?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.32,0:04:44.17,Flashback,Lena,0,0,0,,Don't worry! I'll make sure to bring a guide!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.64,0:04:45.98,Flashback,Philia,0,0,0,,A guide?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.68,0:04:51.13,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why is my guide Prince Osvalt?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.13,0:04:54.83,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,I'm honored to be given \Nthe role of escorting our saint.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.67,0:04:57.69,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Let me show you around Almburg!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.12,0:05:00.69,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,This is the merchant quarter.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.11,0:05:04.40,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,If you're in the market for anything,\Nthis should be your first stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.97,0:05:11.58,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Monster attacks have actually made it hard \Nto leave the city for the past few months.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.00,0:05:15.25,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,But that's all in the past now thanks to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.25,0:05:17.54,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Everyone's so happy the city's thriving again.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.32,0:05:19.87,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,I'm happy, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.35,0:05:21.83,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,All because of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.83,0:05:22.92,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Thank you so much.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.55,0:05:27.34,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}He thanked me?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.84,0:05:30.05,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've just been doing my job...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.06,0:05:34.27,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why does it feel like my heart's racing?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.61,0:05:38.81,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Is something the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.81,0:05:40.07,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,Oh, nothing!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.07,0:05:41.90,Default,Son,0,0,0,,Hey, it's the saint!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.52,0:05:44.07,Default,Merchant,0,0,0,,Saint Philia?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.53,0:05:47.15,Default,Merchant,0,0,0,,I had no idea you were in Parnacorta...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.72,0:05:49.36,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,I know you, don't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.36,0:05:50.07,Default,Merchant,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.63,0:05:54.64,Default,Merchant,0,0,0,,I made an appeal to you \Nonce back in Girtonia.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.64,0:05:58.00,Default,Merchant,0,0,0,,Thanks to you, I've been \Nable to keep up my trade.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.00,0:06:01.14,Default,Merchant,0,0,0,,This is my son. Say hello.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.14,0:06:02.09,Default,Son,0,0,0,,Hello.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.43,0:06:04.55,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Hello.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.18,0:06:10.14,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, no. I'm going to scare someone again.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.14,0:06:12.62,Default,Son,0,0,0,,Thank you, Saint Philia.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.62,0:06:16.02,Default,Son,0,0,0,,My dad was real sad that he \Ncouldn't work for so long.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.02,0:06:17.80,Default,Son,0,0,0,,So thanks a bunch!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.85,0:06:22.25,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Y-You're... welcome?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.25,0:06:23.09,Default,Son,0,0,0,,Thanks!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.01,0:06:26.49,Default,People,0,0,0,,It's the saint!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.49,0:06:29.63,Default,People,0,0,0,,Thank you so much for coming to Parnacorta!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.63,0:06:31.57,Default,People,0,0,0,,Coming all the way from Girtonia...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.57,0:06:33.15,Default,People,0,0,0,,They're feeding you well, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.15,0:06:34.62,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,U-Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.94,0:06:40.79,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.22,0:06:44.92,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Sorry, everyone! I've got dibs for today!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.07,0:06:48.03,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,Good job, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.28,0:06:51.30,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Sorry I startled you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.30,0:06:53.68,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,It's not much by way of apology,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.68,0:06:55.65,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,but please order anything you'd like.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.65,0:06:57.54,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,The desserts here are delicious.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.22,0:07:00.99,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,What's your favorite kind?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.99,0:07:02.16,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,My favorite?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.81,0:07:05.82,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnArial\fs20\c&HB05776&\b1\3c&HF7FBF6&\bord3\shad0\4c&HA76865&\move(541.323,252,185,252)}"Whatever's edible" mindset
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.30,0:07:10.56,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,If you're not sure, may I \Nmake some recommendations?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.56,0:07:13.20,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Oh, yes. Please do.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.08,0:07:20.42,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Th-This is all so alien.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.42,0:07:22.85,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}How am I to act in this situation?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.85,0:07:23.93,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Miss Philia...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.12,0:07:29.50,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Let me thank you again for all \Nthe effort you've put in this week.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.39,0:07:34.76,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,But I've also received reports \Nthat you're overworking yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.76,0:07:37.72,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Miss Philia, rest is also part of the job.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.51,0:07:42.44,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's... part of my job?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.88,0:07:45.95,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,I think you should take \Nmore time for yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.62,0:07:47.69,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,To that end...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.40,0:07:50.11,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Tell me more about you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.60,0:07:54.58,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,What you like, what you dislike, \Nyour interests... Anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.58,0:07:59.29,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,I want to know not just our saint,\Nbut Philia Adenauer herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.74,0:08:00.79,Main - Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,My!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.87,0:08:05.38,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't know how to respond to that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.99,0:08:06.79,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}After all...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.37,0:08:12.30,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've never had space to have my \Nown thoughts about anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.84,0:08:16.22,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wasn't really allowed to.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.87,0:08:24.74,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}What a fine, calming aroma...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.35,0:08:26.31,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.09,0:08:30.07,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,I like tea.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.68,0:08:35.93,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I guess that's okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.58,0:08:43.33,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,But I can't tell you more, \Nbecause I really don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.65,0:08:46.91,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Then let's feel it out little by little.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.91,0:08:50.00,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,I know! Is there anywhere \Nyou'd like to go next?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.00,0:08:51.46,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,I'll take you anywhere you want.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.69,0:08:57.04,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Well... may I make a request?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.98,0:08:59.93,Main - Italics,Lena,0,0,0,,Here we go!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.58,0:09:05.00,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Might I have permission to read the \Nrestricted books in the castle library?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.84,0:09:10.49,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,What are you trying to find out?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.49,0:09:14.75,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,The sheer quantity of monsters \Nappearing in Parnacorta lately
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.75,0:09:18.32,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,can't be explained merely by geography \Nand the prior absence of a saint.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.29,0:09:23.88,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,A similar phenomenon was beginning \Nin Girtonia just before I came here.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.65,0:09:26.50,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,This sudden surge in monsters...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.50,0:09:31.94,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,I've seen such happenings chronicled \Nin old Girtonian history books.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.94,0:09:33.92,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,You seem to have similar records.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.40,0:09:38.66,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,If my hypothesis is correct,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.66,0:09:41.18,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,the Demon Realm is approaching the surface.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.12,0:09:44.93,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,So you're saying...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.96,0:09:47.77,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,What, exactly?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.77,0:09:51.90,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oh, that's right. I guess I have to explain!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.26,0:09:57.46,Default,Lena,0,0,0,,{\i1}Saint Philia... this is nowhere near a date!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.71,0:09:57.99,Default,Sign,0,0,0,,{\an2\fnGeorgia\b1\fs10\shad0\bord0\c&H884FD9&\pos(323,110)}The Too-Perfect Saint{\c&H9B9999&}: {\c&HDEC58D&}Tossed {\c&HDDBF93&}Aside\N{\c&HE2B99A&}by {\c&HC8ACAD&}My {\c&HDDB3B4&}Fiancé {\c&HDCBAC3&}and {\c&HD79BB3&}Sold {\c&HCEA8CE&}to {\c&HD4A8D5&}Another {\c&HC3A8E2&}Kingdom
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.16,0:10:01.52,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,Four hundred years ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.52,0:10:04.56,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,there was a time the Demon Realm \Ncame close to the surface world.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.56,0:10:07.54,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,Monsters invaded us, running rampant.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.54,0:10:10.04,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,The archdemon Asmodeus took \Nadvantage of the chaos
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.04,0:10:14.92,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,to rise from the depths of the\N Demon Realm and come to the surface.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.88,0:10:18.39,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,Humans and animals were \Nslaughtered en masse,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.39,0:10:21.34,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,and many kingdoms faced \Nthe threat of destruction.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.34,0:10:22.55,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,But just then...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.01,0:10:27.00,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,A saint rose up to oppose Asmodeus.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.82,0:10:31.36,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,Her name was Fianna Aesfill,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.36,0:10:35.57,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,and she would later be known\N as Archsaint Fianna.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.36,0:10:41.07,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,She created massive barriers to purge \Nthe monsters in the blink of an eye,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.53,0:10:46.43,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,then separated Asmodeus's soul\Nfrom his supposedly invincible body
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.43,0:10:47.58,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,and sealed it away.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.96,0:10:52.64,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,Thus, peace was restored to the land
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.64,0:10:54.90,Main - Italics,Philia,0,0,0,,and history continues to this day.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.35,0:11:00.29,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,You're saying we're facing \Nanother such crisis?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.29,0:11:03.43,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Yes. I believe it's highly likely.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.10,0:11:07.67,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}The prince called a full conference \Nin response to my supposition.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.32,0:11:12.94,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's asking for the opinions \Nof others as well...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.94,0:11:15.69,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,What precisely happens as \Nthe Demon Realm gets closer?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.69,0:11:19.99,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,The spawning of monsters will likely \Nincrease between ten and twentyfold.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.99,0:11:21.96,Default,Bjorn,0,0,0,,T-Twentyfold?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.96,0:11:24.85,Default,Bjorn,0,0,0,,It's hard enough to keep \Nthem at bay as it is!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.85,0:11:25.91,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.91,0:11:30.04,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Which means the pillars of light\N may no longer be enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.04,0:11:33.94,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,So we'll have to call in the military?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.94,0:11:39.05,Default,Chancellor,0,0,0,,But to increase our defense budget \Nbased on such thin speculation...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.57,0:11:41.27,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.27,0:11:46.22,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's natural they wouldn't believe a girl \Nfrom another kingdom who only just arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.47,0:11:49.48,Flashback,Julius,0,0,0,,Know your place, woman! It's shameful!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.92,0:11:55.18,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,All right. Let's see if tripling\N the defense budget does the trick.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.40,0:12:00.76,Default,Chancellor,0,0,0,,B-But our budget this year\Nis already so tight—
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.83,0:12:01.95,Main - Top,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Budgets are just budgets.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.95,0:12:04.33,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Let's talk my father and my brother into it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.33,0:12:05.72,Default,Chancellor,0,0,0,,But—
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.72,0:12:08.70,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,I'm hoping this is all unnecessary, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.70,0:12:11.75,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,But it's better to be prepared \Nthan to regret it later.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.11,0:12:14.30,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,I'll take responsibility for everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.30,0:12:17.31,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,I'm putting my full faith behind Miss Philia.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.88,0:12:21.69,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,She's done so much for us, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.69,0:12:24.73,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,It's only polite to pay \Nher back with our trust.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.73,0:12:26.33,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Any objections?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.50,0:12:31.27,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}How can he be so confident?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.93,0:12:34.32,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is he not afraid of rebuke?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.87,0:12:40.07,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Even if he's royalty, there must surely be \Nconsequences for wasting treasury funds...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.34,0:12:44.07,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is there any way I can help him?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.41,0:12:49.49,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,These are the forces and locations\N we can rally on short notice.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.49,0:12:50.83,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,Will this do?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.83,0:12:52.51,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,It's not nearly enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.51,0:12:53.29,Default,Soldier,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.29,0:12:55.80,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,This will spell a great deal of casualties.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.80,0:12:57.24,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,That's rough...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.24,0:12:59.04,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,We only have so many soldiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.03,0:13:02.05,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's a way to do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.42,0:13:04.18,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}But if I go through with it...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.65,0:13:10.03,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}My priority right now
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.03,0:13:12.64,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}is protecting the people of Parnacorta.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.15,0:13:16.63,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,There's something else we can try.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.88,0:13:21.32,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,We could erect a Great Purification \NCircle over the entire kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.62,0:13:23.38,Default,Bjorn,0,0,0,,A Great Purification Circle?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.15,0:13:27.93,Default,Bjorn,0,0,0,,B-But that's an ancient ritual.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.93,0:13:32.12,Default,Bjorn,0,0,0,,Without mastery of archaic languages and\Nfull understanding of several spell lineages...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.12,0:13:33.08,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,I can do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.08,0:13:36.90,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,This magic circle doesn't have the caging \Nproperties of a standard barrier.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.90,0:13:39.78,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,It's fully focused on weakening monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.46,0:13:45.80,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnArial\fs16\shad0\b1\pos(164.808,250)\c&H111918&\3c&H9BCBD1&}Standard Barrier
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.46,0:13:45.80,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fnArial\fs16\shad0\b1\c&H111918&\3c&H9BCBD1&\pos(453.305,250)}Great Purification Circle
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.78,0:13:44.39,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Its purifying power will allow any within it\Nto be disposed of with ease.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.98,0:13:45.80,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.15,0:13:48.37,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Is there a catch?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.37,0:13:49.05,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.53,0:13:51.89,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,To erect a Great Purification Circle,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.89,0:13:54.04,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,I must remain at its center,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.04,0:13:56.56,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,acting as the ritual's core.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.58,0:13:56.58,Default,Sign,0,0,0,,{\shad1\bord1\an1\fs14\fnArial\fad(120,1)\c&H182021&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&H738182&\pos(405.846,209.231)}Capital City\NAlmburg\N(Current location)
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.04,0:14:00.01,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Effectively, I will have \Nto remain in the capital.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.56,0:14:02.21,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,In other words, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.07,0:14:07.45,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,I won't be able to do most of \Nthe jobs I've been performing so far.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.48,0:14:13.45,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Er... is that all?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.47,0:14:15.41,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.70,0:14:18.58,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Well, that sounds great, then!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.12,0:14:21.42,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,You work too hard as it is!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.42,0:14:27.11,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Actually, will maintaining the ritual \Nbe exhausting in its own right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.11,0:14:31.39,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,No, once successfully activated, \Nit shouldn't prove draining at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.39,0:14:35.92,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Then this sounds like the perfect solution!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.65,0:14:46.70,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Looks like you're saving our \Nkingdom yet again, Miss Philia.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.97,0:14:49.82,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,What's wrong? You look unhappy.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.82,0:14:52.48,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Is something else weighing on your mind?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.48,0:14:54.16,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Well, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.65,0:14:57.44,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,I'm thinking of my sister back home.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.44,0:14:59.00,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Miss Mia?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.00,0:14:59.66,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.32,0:15:02.72,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,She's an excellent saint,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.72,0:15:05.32,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,but she has no knowledge of ancient rituals.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.32,0:15:08.17,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,She won't be able to create \Na Great Purification Circle.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.74,0:15:10.72,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,And you're worried about her?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.63,0:15:16.24,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Ah, p-please forgive me, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.24,0:15:19.40,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,I'm Parnacorta's saint. I shouldn't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.40,0:15:21.23,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,No need to apologize.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.57,0:15:24.32,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,What kind of big sister wouldn't be worried?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.76,0:15:27.16,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,Don't hold back.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.16,0:15:28.40,Default,Osvalt,0,0,0,,You can help her out.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.72,0:15:31.81,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,In that case...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.06,0:15:34.14,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,May I...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.04,0:15:37.53,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,May I send her a letter?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.95,0:15:42.92,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I simply can't accept this!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.33,0:15:48.00,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}My sister would never leave the \Nkingdom without a word to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.25,0:15:52.82,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mother and Father insist \Nthat it's what she wanted.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.82,0:15:54.08,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Which means...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.13,0:15:59.13,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I should ask her fiancé, \NPrince Julius, about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.13,0:16:02.06,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}They say he wept as he watched her go, so...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.52,0:16:04.72,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Prince Julius.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.72,0:16:06.23,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,I believe you wanted to see me?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.23,0:16:07.52,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,What do you—
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.24,0:16:09.78,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Mia Adenauer!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.90,0:16:12.78,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Will you please become my wife?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.05,0:16:14.78,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.10,0:16:17.17,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Such beauty! Such grace!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.17,0:16:20.33,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,You're a more than worthy bride \Nfor the second prince of Girtonia!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.72,0:16:22.94,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}What in the world is he talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.94,0:16:27.17,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}On the heels of losing his fiancée, \Nhe's already proposing to another girl?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.17,0:16:28.84,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}And her little sister, at that?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.80,0:16:31.59,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}How absolutely disgusting.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.57,0:16:33.47,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Wait...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.95,0:16:37.60,Flashback,Cornelia,0,0,0,,If Philia marries the prince, \Nwe'll get in good with the court!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.60,0:16:42.06,Flashback,George,0,0,0,,You could say she's finally \Ndoing right by the family!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.06,0:16:46.52,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}The reason they're both so\N indifferent to her departure...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.52,0:16:48.57,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did they know about this?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.57,0:16:51.07,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Come on! Let's have your answer!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.75,0:16:52.99,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}In your dreams.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.66,0:16:56.28,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}But if I want to know what really happened,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.28,0:16:58.78,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I need to get him to tell me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.30,0:17:00.82,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have to do this!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.40,0:17:03.94,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Mia?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.94,0:17:05.46,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Highness...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.46,0:17:08.63,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Please give me some time to think it over.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.63,0:17:10.67,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,My sister's only just departed.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.67,0:17:12.96,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,I surely couldn't agree to marry so soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.96,0:17:15.84,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,R-Right, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.84,0:17:19.22,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,I suppose I've been a bit hasty, haven't I?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.53,0:17:22.86,Main - Top,Julius,0,0,0,,In that case, let's give it some time.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.88,0:17:22.86,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can't afford to cross him just yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.86,0:17:24.73,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have to suppress my true feelings.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.73,0:17:27.52,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}It wouldn't do to accept\N the proposal so quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.52,0:17:30.37,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll distract him, throw him off,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.37,0:17:32.48,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}and draw out the information I want.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.48,0:17:34.72,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm not strategically minded at all...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.72,0:17:37.78,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}But for my sister, I'll do whatever I must!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.28,0:17:41.13,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,I'm simply delighted, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.13,0:17:43.76,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}If he thinks I'm nothing \Nbut sunshine and smiles,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.76,0:17:45.29,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}he's got another thing coming!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.63,0:17:52.30,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}That was the day I began \Nmy investigation in earnest.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.73,0:17:54.30,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}In my father's study,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.30,0:17:58.30,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I found plans for a new mansion\Nand a pile of contract documents.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.85,0:18:02.93,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}In my mother's room, \NI found a new box of jewelry.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.49,0:18:06.95,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Philia was such a bore to be around!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.95,0:18:10.61,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I grit my teeth through dates \Nto get on the prince's good side,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.98,0:18:13.89,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}all while keeping up my saintly duties.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.89,0:18:17.72,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}The monsters are only increasing\Nin number with my sister gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.72,0:18:20.32,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's taking everything I have\N to stave them off.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.32,0:18:20.99,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}But...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.86,0:18:25.62,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,I'll do the best I can.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.17,0:18:27.15,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Big Sister...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.54,0:18:34.86,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,What in the world is taking Mia so long?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.37,0:18:38.00,Default,Cornelia,0,0,0,,What if His Highness changes his mind?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.67,0:18:39.43,Default,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(400,1)\an1\pos(29.285,235.26)\fnArial\shad0\b1\fs20\c&H363634&\3c&HFCFEFE&}From Philia
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.00,0:18:40.66,Default,George,0,0,0,,Please. No need to worry there.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.30,0:18:47.08,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}Today's the day I'll lower\Nhis guard and get him to talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.08,0:18:50.18,Default,Noble A,0,0,0,,Marquess Adenauer's quite \Na wily one, isn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.69,0:18:56.07,Default,Noble B,0,0,0,,He offloaded a burden, made a tidy profit,\Nand earned a peerage in the process!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.07,0:19:03.07,Default,Noble A,0,0,0,,And didn't he and Prince Julius look tickled \Nconcocting that plan to sell Saint Philia off?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.38,0:19:05.99,Default,Noble B,0,0,0,,I know our old saint was utterly obnoxious...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.45,0:19:10.25,Default,Noble B,0,0,0,,But how sad to think her fiancé  \Nand parents hated her, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.34,0:19:13.67,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}What are they talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.67,0:19:18.30,Default,Noble A,0,0,0,,Impressive that they pulled it off \Nwhile the king was laid up sick.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.30,0:19:22.09,Default,Noble A,0,0,0,,The marquess was handsomely \Nrewarded, wasn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.09,0:19:25.18,Default,Noble B,0,0,0,,He's apparently using that\N to fund a new estate.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.18,0:19:26.56,Default,Noble B,0,0,0,,Some men get all the luck!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.56,0:19:28.57,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's all coming together.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.57,0:19:31.43,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}They sold my sister...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.86,0:19:39.78,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wanted to believe that my \Nparents were good people.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.51,0:19:43.86,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I had my questions about \Nthe way they treated my sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.86,0:19:45.27,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}But I...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.70,0:19:50.92,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was afraid to see the truth,\N so I blinded myself!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.54,0:19:52.47,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Big Sister!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.68,0:19:57.49,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Have you lived your whole life \Nin a world this cold to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.60,0:20:01.09,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,I'm sorry...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.09,0:20:04.51,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Philia!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.69,0:20:09.85,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Is today the day you finally accept my offer?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.34,0:20:11.60,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Your Highness...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.60,0:20:15.81,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Did my sister really go \Nto Parnacorta of her own free will?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.52,0:20:19.23,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Do we have to go over this again?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.77,0:20:25.49,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Philia chose to break \Nour engagement and leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.49,0:20:28.68,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Just what you'd expect from her, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.68,0:20:32.48,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,She loves nothing more\N than showing off her talents!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.48,0:20:36.70,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,I already had my hands full \Nwith the terrible way she carried on.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.70,0:20:40.51,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,I mean, I was her fiancé!\N I was the one getting all the complaints!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.51,0:20:44.70,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Meanwhile, Mia, you just focus on \Nyour saintly duties instead of
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.70,0:20:47.01,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,sticking your nose where it doesn't belong.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.01,0:20:52.52,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Everyone loves your beauty \Nand your charming smile!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.27,0:20:59.15,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,I happen to believe that you're {\i1}really{\i0}\N the greatest saint of all time.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.15,0:21:02.56,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,I went along with them giving \Nthat title to Philia,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.56,0:21:06.74,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,but she's fatally lacking in charm!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.74,0:21:11.20,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Have faith in yourself! \NYou've already surpassed her!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.20,0:21:12.20,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.20,0:21:14.83,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Hey, don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.83,0:21:20.59,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Philia's the saint of a neighboring \Nkingdom, living her new life!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.59,0:21:25.29,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,I'm sure she'd want her\Ndear younger sister to be happy!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.22,0:21:28.37,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Highness...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.84,0:21:32.47,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,I accept your proposal!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.64,0:21:34.58,Default,Julius,0,0,0,,Really?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.58,0:21:35.24,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.03,0:21:38.53,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll get engaged to this man.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.03,0:21:38.98,Main - Top,Julius,0,0,0,,Yes, of course you do!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.53,0:21:41.68,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll take him to the heights of ecstasy, \Ngive him a long leash,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.68,0:21:44.28,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}and then, when I deem the time to be right...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.28,0:21:45.86,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll betray him.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.70,0:21:52.06,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}After all, he has to be punished \Nfor betraying my sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.02,0:21:55.00,Default,Mia,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's how it has to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.88,0:23:32.97,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Too-Perfect Saint: Tossed Aside by \NMy Fiancé and Sold to Another Kingdom{\i0}.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.76,0:23:35.80,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,Next time, episode 4:
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.01,0:23:40.02,Default,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\shad1\bord0\fs18\fnGeorgia\c&HFBFFFF&\3c&H4E4E4E&\4c&H6A6763&\pos(320,67.102)\b1}Next Time
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.01,0:23:40.02,Default,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\shad1\bord0\fs14\fnGeorgia\c&HFBFFFF&\3c&H4E4E4E&\4c&H6A6763&\b1\pos(320,120.348)}Episode 4
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.01,0:23:40.02,Default,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\shad1\bord0\an8\fnGeorgia\c&HFBFFFF&\3c&H4E4E4E&\fs20\4c&H6A6763&\b1\pos(320,242.204)}"Feelings {\fs24\c&HCCC930&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Entrusted{\fs20\c&HFBFFFF&\4c&H6A6763&}"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.37,0:23:37.67,Default,Philia,0,0,0,,"Feelings Entrusted."
